<http://data.silknow.org/object/76904737-d32b-3ac9-9e68-136a1748e20e/observation/3>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "The oldest Ottoman embroideries in the V&A date from the 16th and 17th centuries.  They are either whole covers and wall hangings or fragments of them. They are decorated with large-scale, bold designs in red, blue, green and yellow, with some white and black. The oldest patterns, such as this one, are made from intersecting lines or lattice which enclose spaces filled with flowers."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/76904737-d32b-3ac9-9e68-136a1748e20e> .

